// Mailpit, comprehensively: servirtium-vcr's pre-recorded/from-testcontainers
// "Pattern for comprehensive suites" (README) applied to Mailpit v1.20 (MIT),
// after the CouchDB pilot.
//
// Two describe blocks, two sets of tapes:
//
// 1. "modules/mailpit": ported from testcontainers-go modules/mailpit/mailpit_test.go,
//    by way of testcontainers-ae's tests/test_mailpit.ae (moved here 2026-11-07).
//    It tests the MODULE (SMTP and HTTP endpoints, smtp_auth, message_limit):
//    one container per case, the original representative tapes.
//
// 2. "Mailpit REST API": written for servirtium-vcr. Re-usable recordings of
//    Mailpit's REST API (and its health endpoints), one tape per scenario, for
//    any language's tests to replay with no Mailpit. This is the comprehensive
//    part. Component-level tests of Mailpit's API, never "end-to-end": the
//    tapes stand in for Mailpit.
//
// PORTING: this file is the reference for what each tape holds; the tapes are
// the re-usable part. A port is a test in your language and test framework
// that makes the same requests in the same order against a Servirtium replay
// server loaded with the tape, and checks the same things. Every request is
// plain HTTP/1.1 with these headers and no others:
//   User-Agent: testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)
//   Content-Type: application/json   (only when there is a body)
// Playback is strict about method, path (query string included, exactly as
// written here), the recorded request headers and the body (byte for byte:
// send the JSON bodies exactly as written in this file, no spaces), and fails
// a case whose recorded requests are not all made. Host, Connection and
// Content-Length are on the tapes but are transport headers, not compared.
//
// Login
// -----
// There is none. Mailpit's UI and API are open unless it is started with
// MP_UI_AUTH (HTTP Basic), which this module does not set, so these tapes
// carry no credential and need no "already logged in" fixture (the way the
// TiDB and Dind suites need none). Credentials never appear on a tape because
// none are used; the SMTP-auth case of the module block is TCP and live only.
//
// Mail in, mail out
// -----------------
// Most cases make their mail ON the tape with Mailpit's own Send API
// (POST /api/v1/send), so each tape is self-contained and replays with nothing
// but HTTP. One case, receives_a_multipart_mail_over_smtp_and_serves_it,
// shows mail that arrived over SMTP (envelope Bcc, the Received header, a
// sender's own Message-ID). SMTP is TCP: the recorder only proxies HTTP, so
// the SMTP conversation is part of the case's live setup (the `live()`
// branch) and is not on the tape; a port that replays the tape sends no mail
// and needs no container.
//
// Every case starts from an empty mailbox (a live run clears it first,
// unrecorded: DELETE /api/v1/messages) and, being independent, leaves it
// empty or at least needs nothing of the others. Message ids, and the tags
// and subjects the cases make, are fixed names so a tape replays alone.
//
// What varies between runs, and what the tapes do with it
// --------------------------------------------------------
// Every rule is registered in api_rules() below, with its reason; the
// "## [Recording rules]" table at the end of each tape lists them and the
// interactions each touched. In short:
//   - normalized ({{id-N}}, the same token wherever the value recurs, because a
//     client sends it back in /message/<id> and {"IDs":[..]}): a message's id.
//   - collapsed (one constant; nobody sends them back): the generated
//     Message-ID (".. @mailpit"), the Send API's MIME boundaries, every time
//     (Created, Date, and the RFC 5322 Date header), the Received header
//     Mailpit adds to mail taken over SMTP (it names the recording machine),
//     the message Size, and the Content-Security-Policy nonce.
//   - left out: Date (response header), as everywhere.
// PORTING: in playback a normalized value comes back as its token, verbatim
// ("{{id-1}}"); treat the id as an opaque string (never assert its length or
// shape) and send it back exactly as received. Send the braces as they are:
// playback compares paths after RFC 3986 normalization, so `{{id-1}}` and
// its percent-encoded form (%7B%7Bid-1%7D%7D) both match. Mailpit answers raw
// messages and attachments with CR LF line ends; the tapes keep the CRs and
// playback serves them as recorded. The assertions ignore CRs (lf() below),
// which is harmless.
//
// Awkward points
// --------------
// None of Mailpit's lists is unordered: messages come newest first, tags and
// search results likewise in a fixed order, JSON keys sorted. The cases send
// their mails one request after another, so "newest first" is the reverse of
// the send order (a mail sent in the same millisecond as another could swap;
// each send is a separate HTTP round trip, so this has not happened). Nothing
// here needs the opt-in stable ordering being added to Servirtium's core.
//
// In and out of scope
// -------------------
// In: the health endpoints (/livez, /readyz) and the web UI configuration;
// the Send API (HTML and text bodies, Cc, Bcc, custom headers, tags,
// attachments); listing, paging (start, limit) and searching (subject:,
// from:, tag:, has:attachment, is:read, is:unread, free text), deleting by
// search; one message in full, its headers, raw text and parts (attachments);
// mark read and unread (some or all); tags (set, list, rename, delete, search
// by tag); deleting some or all messages; mail received over SMTP (as live
// setup); the representative errors 400 and 404.
// Out: webhooks and anything pushed (the websocket at /api/events, the live
// UI: connections, not messages), releasing a message to an SMTP relay and
// the relay's allow-lists (needs a second SMTP server), the SpamAssassin,
// HTML-check and link-check endpoints (they need SpamAssassin, a network and
// a compatibility database; link-check fetches URLs), POP3, TLS, the chaos
// SMTP triggers, /api/v1/info (it reports the memory in use, the database
// path and the latest GitHub release: every run differs), thumbnails of
// inline images, message and tag auto-tagging options (environment), and
// the Basic-auth UI (MP_UI_AUTH, not set by the module). Each could be a later case.
//
// Running it (from pre-recorded/from-testcontainers):
//   ae test mailpit/test_mailpit.ae                         container, no Servirtium
//   TCAE_VCR=record   ae test mailpit/test_mailpit.ae       write the tapes
//   TCAE_VCR=check    ae test mailpit/test_mailpit.ae       fail if a tape changed
//   TCAE_VCR=playback ae test mailpit/test_mailpit.ae       no container: the tapes
// The API cases share one container (started on the first one and removed at
// the end); the module cases each start their own.

import std.spec
import std.string
import std.tcp
import std.http.client
import std.json
import testcontainers as tc
import testcontainers.docker
import testcontainers.testing
import servirtium
import modules.mailpit

const IMAGE = "axllent/mailpit:v1.20"

fn last_line(text: string) -> string {
    rest = text
    i = string.index_of(rest, "\n")
    while i >= 0 {
        rest = string.substring(rest, i + 1, string.length(rest))
        i = string.index_of(rest, "\n")
    }
    return string.trim(rest)
}

// Read one SMTP reply (possibly multi-line): done when a line starts with
// three digits and a space. Returns the whole reply text.
fn smtp_reply(sock: ptr) -> (string, string) {
    buf = ""
    tries = 0
    while tries < 100 {
        chunk, rerr = tcp.read(sock, 4096)
        if rerr != "" && rerr != "timeout" { return buf, rerr }
        buf = string.concat(buf, chunk)
        if string.ends_with(buf, "\n") == 1 {
            // the last line of the reply: "250 ..." (not "250-...")
            last = last_line(string.trim(buf))
            if string.length(last) >= 4 && string.substring(last, 3, 4) == " " { return buf, "" }
        }
        tries = tries + 1
    }
    return buf, "no complete SMTP reply: ${buf}"
}

fn smtp_cmd(sock: ptr, line: string, expect: string) -> string {
    _, werr = tcp.write(sock, string.concat(line, "\r\n"))
    if werr != "" { return werr }
    rep, rerr = smtp_reply(sock)
    if rerr != "" { return rerr }
    if string.starts_with(rep, expect) == 0 { return "'${line}' expected ${expect}, got: ${rep}" }
    return ""
}

// Send one mail: "" or the error.
fn send_mail(endpoint: string, from: string, to: string, subject: string, body: string) -> string {
    i = string.index_of(endpoint, ":")
    h = string.substring(endpoint, 0, i)
    port, _ = string.to_int(string.substring(endpoint, i + 1, string.length(endpoint)))
    sock, cerr = tcp.connect(h, port)
    if cerr != "" { return "connect ${endpoint}: ${cerr}" }
    banner, berr = smtp_reply(sock)
    if berr != "" || string.starts_with(banner, "220") == 0 { tcp.tcp_close(sock); return "banner: ${banner} ${berr}" }
    e = smtp_cmd(sock, "EHLO tcae.test", "250")
    if e == "" { e = smtp_cmd(sock, "MAIL FROM:<${from}>", "250") }
    if e == "" { e = smtp_cmd(sock, "RCPT TO:<${to}>", "250") }
    if e == "" { e = smtp_cmd(sock, "DATA", "354") }
    if e == "" {
        msg = "From: ${from}\r\nTo: ${to}\r\nSubject: ${subject}\r\n\r\n${body}\r\n."
        e = smtp_cmd(sock, msg, "250")
    }
    if e == "" { e = smtp_cmd(sock, "QUIT", "221") }
    tcp.tcp_close(sock)
    return e
}

// The User-Agent this test's HTTP client sends, as an app's client library
// would: Go's net/http adds `Go-http-client/1.1` by itself, Aether's
// std.http.client adds none. Set here, in the test's own client, so the
// recordings show a representative request; Servirtium records what the
// client sends and adds nothing of its own.
const USER_AGENT = "testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)"

fn http_get(url: string) -> (int, string, string) {
    req = client.request("GET", url)
    client.set_header(req, "User-Agent", USER_AGENT)
    client.set_timeout(req, 5s)
    r, err = client.send_request(req)
    client.request_free(req)
    if err != "" { return 0, "", err }
    status = client.response_status(r)
    body = client.response_body(r)
    client.response_free(r)
    return status, body, ""
}


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The comprehensive "Mailpit REST API" block: helpers
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Send raw message data to several recipients: "" or the error. The envelope
// (RCPT TO) is what Mailpit records as To, Cc and Bcc recipients, so a
// recipient that is in no header is a Bcc. data is the message with LF line
// ends, the dot-stuffing left to the caller (none here).
fn send_raw(endpoint: string, from: string, rcpts: string[], data: string) -> string {
    i = string.index_of(endpoint, ":")
    h = string.substring(endpoint, 0, i)
    port, _ = string.to_int(string.substring(endpoint, i + 1, string.length(endpoint)))
    sock, cerr = tcp.connect(h, port)
    if cerr != "" { return "connect ${endpoint}: ${cerr}" }
    banner, berr = smtp_reply(sock)
    if berr != "" || string.starts_with(banner, "220") == 0 { tcp.tcp_close(sock); return "banner: ${banner} ${berr}" }
    e = smtp_cmd(sock, "EHLO tcae.test", "250")
    if e == "" { e = smtp_cmd(sock, "MAIL FROM:<${from}>", "250") }
    for r in rcpts {
        if e == "" { e = smtp_cmd(sock, "RCPT TO:<${r}>", "250") }
    }
    if e == "" { e = smtp_cmd(sock, "DATA", "354") }
    if e == "" {
        crlf = string.replace_all(data, "\n", "\r\n")
        e = smtp_cmd(sock, "${crlf}\r\n.", "250")
    }
    if e == "" { e = smtp_cmd(sock, "QUIT", "221") }
    tcp.tcp_close(sock)
    return e
}

// A string in a JSON body by a dotted path ("messages.0.ID", "Attachments.0.PartID");
// "" when absent or not a string.
fn jstr(body: string, path: string) -> string {
    doc, err = json.parse(body)
    if err != "" { return "" }
    let v: ptr = doc
    rest = path
    while string.length(rest) > 0 && v != null {
        p = rest
        dot = string.index_of(rest, ".")
        if dot >= 0 {
            p = string.substring(rest, 0, dot)
            rest = string.substring(rest, dot + 1, string.length(rest))
        } else {
            rest = ""
        }
        if json.json_type(v) == json.JSON_ARRAY {
            idx, _ = string.to_int(p)
            a, _ = json.array_get(v, idx)
            v = a
        } else {
            o, _ = json.object_get(v, p)
            v = o
        }
    }
    out = ""
    if v != null {
        s, serr = json.get_string(v)
        if serr == "" { out = string.copy(s) }
    }
    json.free(doc)
    return out
}

// A number in a JSON body by a dotted path, as text ("" when absent): the
// counts a list response carries ("total", "unread", "count").
fn jnum(body: string, path: string) -> string {
    marker = "\"${path}\":"
    i = string.index_of(body, marker)
    if i < 0 { return "" }
    j = i + string.length(marker)
    out = ""
    while j < string.length(body) {
        ch = string.char_at(body, j)
        if ch < 48 || ch > 57 { return out }
        out = string.concat(out, string.from_char(ch))
        j = j + 1
    }
    return out
}

fn lf(body: string) -> string {
    return string.replace_all(body, "\r", "")
}

var api: string = ""
var smtp_addr: string = ""

// One request to the API: (status, body). A transport error fails the case.
// No credentials: Mailpit's UI and API are open unless MP_UI_AUTH is set.
fn mp(method: string, path: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    req = client.request(method, "${api}${path}")
    client.set_header(req, "User-Agent", USER_AGENT)
    client.set_timeout(req, 30s)
    if string.length(body) > 0 { client.set_body(req, string.bytes(body), "application/json") }
    r, err = client.send_request(req)
    client.request_free(req)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "${method} ${path}")
    if err != "" { return 0, "" }
    st = client.response_status(r)
    b = client.response_body(r)
    client.response_free(r)
    return st, b
}

// The Send API's request for a message: alice to bob with the given subject
// and tags (a JSON array text such as "[\"a\",\"b\"]", or "[]").
fn send_body(subject: string, text: string, tags: string) -> string {
    return "{\"From\":{\"Email\":\"alice@example.com\",\"Name\":\"Alice\"},\"To\":[{\"Email\":\"bob@example.com\",\"Name\":\"Bob\"}],\"Subject\":\"${subject}\",\"Text\":\"${text}\",\"Tags\":${tags}}"
}

// POST /api/v1/send and return the new message's id.
fn send_mail_api(subject: string, text: string, tags: string) -> string {
    st, b = mp("POST", "/api/v1/send", send_body(subject, text, tags))
    spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "send ${subject}: ${b}")
    return jstr(b, "ID")
}

var shared_container: ptr = null
var shared_base: string = ""

// The shared Mailpit's base URL, starting it on first use ("" on failure).
fn shared() -> string {
    if string.length(shared_base) > 0 { return shared_base }
    c, err = mailpit.run(IMAGE)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "mailpit starts")
    if err != "" { return "" }
    shared_container = c as ptr
    s, e1 = mailpit.smtp_endpoint(c)
    spec.assert_ok(e1, "smtp endpoint")
    b, e2 = mailpit.http_url(c)
    spec.assert_ok(e2, "http url")
    smtp_addr = s
    shared_base = b
    return shared_base
}

// Start an API case: in a live mode, the shared Mailpit with an empty mailbox
// (DELETE /api/v1/messages, unrecorded), then the recording. Sets `api`;
// returns the recording handle, and ok = 0 when the case cannot run.
fn begin(case_: string) -> (ptr, int) {
    addr = ""
    if servirtium.live() == 1 {
        addr = shared()
        if addr == "" { return null, 0 }
        req = client.request("DELETE", "${addr}/api/v1/messages")
        client.set_header(req, "User-Agent", USER_AGENT)
        client.set_timeout(req, 30s)
        r, err = client.send_request(req)
        client.request_free(req)
        spec.assert_ok(err, "empty the mailbox (not recorded)")
        if err == "" { client.response_free(r) }
    }
    base, rec = servirtium.recording("mailpit", case_, addr)
    api = base
    return rec, 1
}

// The module cases' rules.
fn module_rules() {
    servirtium.clear_rules()
    // What differs run to run, none of it sent back by the test: the message's
    // ID and Message-ID, its Created time, and the nonce in the response's
    // Content-Security-Policy header.
    servirtium.collapse("\"ID\":\"[A-Za-z0-9]{22}\"", "\"ID\":\"MESSAGE-ID\"")
    servirtium.collapse("\"MessageID\":\"[A-Za-z0-9]+@mailpit\"", "\"MessageID\":\"MESSAGE-ID@mailpit\"")
    servirtium.collapse(servirtium.RFC3339, "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z")
    // The message's Size in bytes, which includes the generated Message-ID
    // header (21 or 22 characters, depending on the run).
    servirtium.collapse("\"Size\":[0-9]+", "\"Size\":0")
    servirtium.collapse("nonce-[A-Za-z0-9]{22}", "nonce-NONCE")
}

// The API cases' rules. Rules apply to every recording after them, so the two
// blocks each clear and register their own.
fn api_rules() {
    servirtium.clear_rules()
    // A message's id (22 base62 characters): Mailpit makes it, and the client
    // sends it back in paths (/message/<id>) and bodies ({"IDs":[..]}).
    // Normalized, so the same message has the same {{id-N}} in all of them.
    // Scoped to the "ID" field of a response so that no other 22-character
    // word is touched; the value is then replaced wherever it recurs.
    servirtium.normalize("(?<=\"ID\":\")[A-Za-z0-9]{22}(?=\")", "id")
    // The Message-ID Mailpit generates for a mail that has none (the Send API
    // always, SMTP when the sender gave none): 21 or 22 base62 characters
    // and "@mailpit", in the list ("MessageID":"..."), in the raw message and
    // in the headers ("Message-Id"). Nobody sends it back: collapsed. Mails
    // sent over SMTP here give a fixed Message-ID, which is left alone.
    servirtium.collapse("[A-Za-z0-9]{21,22}@mailpit", "MESSAGE-ID@mailpit")
    // The Send API's MIME boundaries are "enmime-<uuid>", random.
    servirtium.collapse(string.concat("enmime-", servirtium.UUID), "enmime-BOUNDARY")
    // Times: Created, Date (RFC 3339, in JSON) and the RFC 5322 Date header
    // (in raw messages and the headers listing). Collapsed: nobody sends
    // them back (a search by date would, and none is made).
    servirtium.collapse(servirtium.RFC3339, "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z")
    servirtium.collapse("(Mon|Tue|Wed|Thu|Fri|Sat|Sun), [0-9]{2} [A-Z][a-z]{2} [0-9]{4} [0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2} [+-][0-9]{4}", "Sat, 01 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000")
    // The Received header Mailpit adds to a mail it takes over SMTP: the
    // sender's host name, the container id and address, and the time. Hostile
    // to a tape (it names the machine that recorded it), and no client sends
    // it back. Collapsed whole (one line, so the rules table stays a table),
    // in the raw message and in the JSON headers.
    servirtium.collapse("(?s)Received: from .*?\\(UTC\\)", "Received: from CLIENT by CONTAINER (Mailpit) with SMTP; Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000 (UTC)")
    servirtium.collapse("(?s)\"Received\":\\[\"from .*?\\(UTC\\)\"\\]", "\"Received\":[\"from CLIENT by CONTAINER (Mailpit) with SMTP; Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000 (UTC)\"]")
    // The message's Size in bytes: it includes the Received header and any
    // generated Message-ID, whose lengths vary.
    servirtium.collapse("\"Size\":[0-9]+", "\"Size\":0")
    // The nonce in every response's Content-Security-Policy header.
    servirtium.collapse("nonce-[A-Za-z0-9]{22}", "nonce-NONCE")
}

main() {
    fw = spec.init()
    if servirtium.skip_if_no_engine(fw) == 1 { return spec.run_summary(fw) }

    module_rules()
    spec.describe(fw, "modules/mailpit") {
        spec.after_each() callback { testing.cleanup_all() }

        spec.it("receives a mail over SMTP and serves it over HTTP (TestMailpit)") callback {
            base = ""
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                c, err = mailpit.run(IMAGE)
                testing.cleanup_container(c)
                spec.assert_ok(err, "mailpit starts")
                if err != "" { return }
                smtp, e1 = mailpit.smtp_endpoint(c)
                spec.assert_ok(e1, "smtp endpoint")
                b, e2 = mailpit.http_url(c)
                spec.assert_ok(e2, "http url")
                spec.assert_true(string.starts_with(b, "http://") == 1, "an http:// URL: ${b}")
                spec.assert_true(string.contains(smtp, "://") == 0, "smtp endpoint is host:port: ${smtp}")
                se = send_mail(smtp, "sender@example.com", "rcpt@example.com", "Hello from tcae", "the body text")
                spec.assert_ok(se, "SMTP conversation")
                base = b
            }
            rbase, rec = servirtium.recording("mailpit", "receives_a_mail_over_smtp_and_serves_it_over_http", base)
            status, body, herr = http_get("${rbase}/api/v1/messages")
            spec.assert_ok(herr, "GET /api/v1/messages")
            spec.assert_eq(status, 200, "messages API status")
            spec.assert_contains(body, "Hello from tcae", "the subject is in the API's list")
            spec.assert_contains(body, "sender@example.com", "the sender is in the API's list")
            spec.assert_contains(body, "rcpt@example.com", "the recipient is in the API's list")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        spec.it_when(servirtium.live(), "requires authentication with smtp_auth (TestMailpitWithSMTPAuth)", "no container in playback") callback {
            c, err = mailpit.run(IMAGE) {
                smtp_auth("user", "secret")
            }
            testing.cleanup_container(c)
            spec.assert_ok(err, "mailpit starts")
            if err == "" {
                smtp, _ = mailpit.smtp_endpoint(c)
                // without credentials MAIL FROM is refused ("530 5.7.0 Authentication required")
                se = send_mail(smtp, "a@example.com", "b@example.com", "no auth", "x")
                spec.assert_true(string.length(se) > 0, "an unauthenticated send is refused")
                spec.assert_contains(se, "530", "the refusal is 530 authentication required: ${se}")
                _, out, eerr = tc.exec(c, ["sh", "-c", "env | grep ^MP_"])
                spec.assert_ok(eerr, "exec")
                spec.assert_contains(out, "MP_SMTP_AUTH=user:secret", "the credentials are in the env")
                spec.assert_contains(out, "MP_SMTP_AUTH_ALLOW_INSECURE=true", "plaintext auth is allowed")
            }
        }

        spec.it("limits the messages kept with message_limit (TestMailpitWithMessageLimit)") callback {
            base = ""
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                c, err = mailpit.run(IMAGE) {
                    message_limit(2)
                }
                testing.cleanup_container(c)
                spec.assert_ok(err, "mailpit starts")
                if err != "" { return }
                smtp, _ = mailpit.smtp_endpoint(c)
                b, _ = mailpit.http_url(c)
                // Mailpit prunes on a slow timer (minutes), so the effect is not
                // observable in a test; the option is checked in the container's
                // environment and the server must still take mail with it set.
                _, out, eerr = tc.exec(c, ["sh", "-c", "env | grep ^MP_MAX"])
                spec.assert_ok(eerr, "exec")
                spec.assert_contains(out, "MP_MAX_MESSAGES=2", "the limit is in the env")
                se = send_mail(smtp, "s@example.com", "r@example.com", "limited", "b")
                spec.assert_ok(se, "send")
                base = b
            }
            rbase, rec = servirtium.recording("mailpit", "limits_the_messages_kept_with_message_limit", base)
            status, body, herr = http_get("${rbase}/api/v1/messages")
            spec.assert_ok(herr, "GET messages")
            spec.assert_contains(body, "\"total\":1", "the mail arrived")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }
    }

    api_rules()
    spec.describe(fw, "Mailpit REST API") {
        spec.after_each() callback { api = "" }

        // PORTING: the health endpoints and an empty mailbox; the first two
        // have an empty body.
        //   GET /livez           -> 200
        //   GET /readyz          -> 200
        //   GET /api/v1/webui    -> 200 {"Label":"","MessageRelay":{"Enabled":false,..},"SpamAssassin":false,"DuplicatesIgnored":false}
        //   GET /api/v1/messages -> 200 {"total":0,"unread":0,"count":0,"messages_count":0,"start":0,"tags":[],"messages":[]}
        //   GET /api/v1/tags     -> 200 []
        //   GET /api/v1/search?query=anything -> 200 an empty list (total 0)
        spec.it("reports readiness and an empty mailbox") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("reports_readiness_and_an_empty_mailbox")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = mp("GET", "/livez", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "livez: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/readyz", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "readyz: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/webui", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "webui: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"SpamAssassin\":false", "no SpamAssassin")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Enabled\":false", "no relay")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "messages: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "total"), "0", "no messages")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"messages\":[]", "an empty list")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/tags", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "tags: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(string.trim(b), "[]", "no tags")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search?query=anything", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "search: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"messages\":[]", "no matches")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: the Send API (an HTTP way to make a mail; no SMTP), then
        // every way of reading it back. Bcc is a list of addresses.
        //   POST /api/v1/send {"From":{"Email":"alice@example.com","Name":"Alice"},"To":[{"Email":"bob@example.com","Name":"Bob"}],
        //        "Cc":[{"Email":"carol@example.com"}],"Bcc":["dave@example.com"],"Subject":"Hello Bob","Text":"plain body",
        //        "HTML":"<p>html <b>body</b></p>","Tags":["greeting","tcae"],"Headers":{"X-Tcae":"1"},
        //        "Attachments":[{"Content":"aGVsbG8gYXR0YWNobWVudA==","Filename":"note.txt"}]} -> 200 {"ID":{{id-1}}}
        //   GET  /api/v1/messages -> 200 total 1, unread 1, messages[0]: ID, From {Name,Address}, To, Cc, Bcc, Subject,
        //        Tags ["greeting","tcae"], Attachments 1, Snippet "html body"
        //   GET  /api/v1/message/<id> -> 200 the full message: Text "plain body", HTML, Attachments [{PartID "2",
        //        FileName "note.txt", ContentType "text/plain", Size 16}] (reading it marks it read)
        //   GET  /api/v1/message/<id>/headers -> 200 {"Bcc":[..],"Cc":[..],"From":[..],"X-Tags":["greeting, tcae"],"X-Tcae":["1"],..}
        //   GET  /api/v1/message/<id>/raw -> 200 the RFC 5322 text, multipart/mixed with a multipart/alternative
        //   GET  /api/v1/message/<id>/part/2 -> 200 "hello attachment" (Content-Type text/plain,
        //        Content-Disposition filename="note.txt")
        //   GET  /api/v1/message/latest -> 200 the same message, Read true now
        //   GET  /api/v1/messages -> unread 0
        spec.it("sends a mail with the Send API and reads it back every way") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("sends_a_mail_with_the_send_api_and_reads_it_back")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            body = "{\"From\":{\"Email\":\"alice@example.com\",\"Name\":\"Alice\"},\"To\":[{\"Email\":\"bob@example.com\",\"Name\":\"Bob\"}],\"Cc\":[{\"Email\":\"carol@example.com\"}],\"Bcc\":[\"dave@example.com\"],\"Subject\":\"Hello Bob\",\"Text\":\"plain body\",\"HTML\":\"<p>html <b>body</b></p>\",\"Tags\":[\"greeting\",\"tcae\"],\"Headers\":{\"X-Tcae\":\"1\"},\"Attachments\":[{\"Content\":\"aGVsbG8gYXR0YWNobWVudA==\",\"Filename\":\"note.txt\"}]}"
            st, b = mp("POST", "/api/v1/send", body)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "send: ${b}")
            id = jstr(b, "ID")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(id) > 0, "an id")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "total"), "1", "one message")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "unread"), "1", "unread")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.ID"), id, "the one we sent")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.From.Address"), "alice@example.com", "from")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.To.0.Name"), "Bob", "to")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.Cc.0.Address"), "carol@example.com", "cc")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.Bcc.0.Address"), "dave@example.com", "bcc")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.Subject"), "Hello Bob", "subject")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.Tags.1"), "tcae", "tags")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.Snippet"), "html body", "snippet")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Attachments\":1", "one attachment")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/${id}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "message: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Text"), "plain body", "text")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "HTML"), "<p>html <b>body</b></p>", "html")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Attachments.0.FileName"), "note.txt", "attachment name")
            partid = jstr(b, "Attachments.0.PartID")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(partid) > 0, "a part id")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/${id}/headers", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "headers: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"X-Tcae\":[\"1\"]", "the custom header")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"X-Tags\":[\"greeting, tcae\"]", "the tags header")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/${id}/raw", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "raw: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(lf(b), "Subject: Hello Bob\n", "the raw subject")
            spec.assert_contains(lf(b), "Content-Type: multipart/mixed;", "multipart/mixed")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/${id}/part/${partid}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "part: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(lf(b), "hello attachment", "the attachment's bytes")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/latest", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "latest: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "ID"), id, "the same message")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "unread"), "0", "reading marked it read")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: mail that arrives over SMTP, which is TCP and so is part of
        // the live setup, not of the tape: a port's replay sends nothing. The
        // setup sends one multipart mail with RCPT TO for bob, carol and
        // hidden@example.com (a Bcc: in no header), a fixed Message-ID
        // <report-1@tcae.test> and a text/csv attachment. The tape holds the reads:
        //   GET /api/v1/messages -> 200 total 1; messages[0]: MessageID "report-1@tcae.test", To [Bob], Cc [carol],
        //        Bcc [hidden@example.com] (from the envelope), Subject "Quarterly report", Attachments 1
        //   GET /api/v1/message/<id> -> 200: Text "Plain text body", HTML, ReturnPath "alice@example.com",
        //        Attachments [{PartID "2", FileName "report.csv", ContentType "text/csv"}]
        //   GET /api/v1/message/<id>/part/2 -> 200 "a,b\n1,2" ; GET .../raw -> the message with Mailpit's
        //        Received header added (collapsed, it names the sending machine) ; GET .../headers -> includes Received
        // The attachment and the raw text have CR LF line ends (kept on the
        // tape and in replay); the assertions compare with CRs removed.
        spec.it("receives a multipart mail over SMTP and serves it") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("receives_a_multipart_mail_over_smtp_and_serves_it")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                msg = "From: Alice <alice@example.com>\nTo: Bob <bob@example.com>\nCc: carol@example.com\nSubject: Quarterly report\nDate: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000\nMessage-ID: <report-1@tcae.test>\nMIME-Version: 1.0\nContent-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=\"tcae-b1\"\n\n--tcae-b1\nContent-Type: multipart/alternative; boundary=\"tcae-b2\"\n\n--tcae-b2\nContent-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\n\nPlain text body\n--tcae-b2\nContent-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8\n\n<p>HTML <b>body</b></p>\n--tcae-b2--\n--tcae-b1\nContent-Type: text/csv; name=\"report.csv\"\nContent-Disposition: attachment; filename=\"report.csv\"\n\na,b\n1,2\n--tcae-b1--\n"
                se = send_raw(smtp_addr, "alice@example.com", ["bob@example.com", "carol@example.com", "hidden@example.com"], msg)
                spec.assert_ok(se, "SMTP conversation (not recorded)")
            }
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "total"), "1", "one message")
            id = jstr(b, "messages.0.ID")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(id) > 0, "an id")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.MessageID"), "report-1@tcae.test", "the sender's Message-ID is kept")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.To.0.Address"), "bob@example.com", "to")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.Cc.0.Address"), "carol@example.com", "cc")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.Bcc.0.Address"), "hidden@example.com", "bcc, from the envelope")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.Subject"), "Quarterly report", "subject")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Attachments\":1", "one attachment")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/${id}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "message: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(lf(jstr(b, "Text")), "Plain text body", "text")
            spec.assert_str_eq(lf(jstr(b, "HTML")), "<p>HTML <b>body</b></p>", "html")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "ReturnPath"), "alice@example.com", "the envelope sender")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Attachments.0.FileName"), "report.csv", "attachment name")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "Attachments.0.ContentType"), "text/csv", "attachment type")
            partid = jstr(b, "Attachments.0.PartID")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/${id}/part/${partid}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "part: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(string.trim(lf(b)), "a,b\n1,2", "the csv")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/${id}/raw", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "raw: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(lf(b), "Received: from ", "Mailpit's Received header (collapsed on the tape)")
            spec.assert_contains(lf(b), "Message-ID: <report-1@tcae.test>", "the Message-ID")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/${id}/headers", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "headers: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"Subject\":[\"Quarterly report\"]", "the subject header")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: paging and searching, four mails sent by the Send API (all from
        // alice@example.com to bob@example.com; the id of each is {{id-N}}):
        //   POST /api/v1/send  subjects "alpha report" (tag "q1"), "beta report" (tag "q1"), "gamma note", "delta note"
        //        Text bodies "first", "second", "third", "fourth"; "delta note" has an attachment; each -> 200 {"ID":..}
        //   GET /api/v1/messages -> total 4, newest first: delta, gamma, beta, alpha
        //   GET /api/v1/messages?start=0&limit=2 -> count 2 (delta, gamma), total 4; ?start=2&limit=2 -> beta, alpha
        //   GET /api/v1/search?query=subject:report -> beta, alpha (count 2)
        //   GET /api/v1/search?query=tag:q1 -> beta, alpha
        //   GET /api/v1/search?query=gamma -> 1 (free text, matches the subject)
        //   GET /api/v1/search?query=has:attachment -> delta
        //   GET /api/v1/search?query=from:alice@example.com -> 4
        //   GET /api/v1/search?query=is:unread -> 4 ; ?query=nosuchword -> 0
        //   DELETE /api/v1/search?query=subject:note -> 200 "ok" ; GET /api/v1/messages -> total 2 (the reports)
        spec.it("pages through and searches messages") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("pages_through_and_searches_messages")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            send_mail_api("alpha report", "first", "[\"q1\"]")
            send_mail_api("beta report", "second", "[\"q1\"]")
            send_mail_api("gamma note", "third", "[]")
            st, b = mp("POST", "/api/v1/send", "{\"From\":{\"Email\":\"alice@example.com\",\"Name\":\"Alice\"},\"To\":[{\"Email\":\"bob@example.com\",\"Name\":\"Bob\"}],\"Subject\":\"delta note\",\"Text\":\"fourth\",\"Attachments\":[{\"Content\":\"eA==\",\"Filename\":\"x.txt\"}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "send delta: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "total"), "4", "four messages")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.Subject"), "delta note", "newest first")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.3.Subject"), "alpha report", "oldest last")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages?start=0&limit=2", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "count"), "2", "a page of two")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "total"), "4", "of four")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.1.Subject"), "gamma note", "page 1, second")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages?start=2&limit=2", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.Subject"), "beta report", "page 2, first")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.1.Subject"), "alpha report", "page 2, second")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search?query=subject:report", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "search subject: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "count"), "2", "two reports")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.Subject"), "beta report", "newest first")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search?query=tag:q1", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "count"), "2", "two tagged q1: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search?query=gamma", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "count"), "1", "free text: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search?query=has:attachment", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "count"), "1", "has:attachment: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "messages.0.Subject"), "delta note", "the one with the attachment")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search?query=from:alice@example.com", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "count"), "4", "from:: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search?query=is:unread", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "count"), "4", "is:unread: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search?query=nosuchword", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "count"), "0", "no match: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("DELETE", "/api/v1/search?query=subject:note", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete by search: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "total"), "2", "the reports are left: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: read state, with three mails "one", "two", "three" from the Send API.
        //   GET /api/v1/messages -> total 3, unread 3
        //   PUT /api/v1/messages {"IDs":[<one>],"Read":true} -> 200 "ok" ; GET -> unread 2
        //   PUT /api/v1/messages {"IDs":[<one>],"Read":false} -> 200 "ok" ; GET -> unread 3
        //   GET /api/v1/message/<two> -> 200 (reading a message marks it read) ; GET /api/v1/messages -> unread 2
        //   PUT /api/v1/messages {"Read":true} (no IDs: every message) -> 200 "ok" ; GET -> unread 0
        //   GET /api/v1/search?query=is:read -> 3 ; ?query=is:unread -> 0
        spec.it("marks messages read and unread") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("marks_messages_read_and_unread")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            one = send_mail_api("one", "1", "[]")
            two = send_mail_api("two", "2", "[]")
            send_mail_api("three", "3", "[]")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "unread"), "3", "all unread: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("PUT", "/api/v1/messages", "{\"IDs\":[\"${one}\"],\"Read\":true}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "mark one read: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(string.trim(b), "ok", "ok")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "unread"), "2", "two unread: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("PUT", "/api/v1/messages", "{\"IDs\":[\"${one}\"],\"Read\":false}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "mark it unread again: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "unread"), "3", "three unread: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/${two}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "open two: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "unread"), "2", "opening marks read: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("PUT", "/api/v1/messages", "{\"Read\":true}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "mark all read: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "unread"), "0", "none unread: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search?query=is:read", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "count"), "3", "three read: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search?query=is:unread", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "count"), "0", "none unread by search: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: tags, with two mails "red" and "blue" from the Send API (no tags).
        //   PUT /api/v1/tags {"IDs":[<red>],"Tags":["x","y"]} -> 200 "ok"
        //   PUT /api/v1/tags {"IDs":[<blue>],"Tags":["y"]} -> 200 "ok"
        //   GET /api/v1/tags -> 200 ["x","y"] (sorted)
        //   GET /api/v1/search?query=tag:y -> 2 ; ?query=tag:x -> 1
        //   PUT /api/v1/tags/x {"Name":"renamed"} -> 200 "ok" ; GET /api/v1/tags -> ["renamed","y"]
        //   PUT /api/v1/tags {"IDs":[<red>],"Tags":[]} -> 200 "ok" (clears red's tags) ; GET /api/v1/tags -> ["y"]
        //   DELETE /api/v1/tags/y -> 200 "ok" ; GET /api/v1/tags -> []
        //   DELETE /api/v1/tags/nosuch -> 400 "tag not found: nosuch"
        //   (the mails themselves are not deleted: GET /api/v1/messages -> total 2)
        spec.it("tags, renames and untags messages") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("tags_renames_and_untags_messages")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            red = send_mail_api("red", "r", "[]")
            blue = send_mail_api("blue", "b", "[]")
            st, b = mp("PUT", "/api/v1/tags", "{\"IDs\":[\"${red}\"],\"Tags\":[\"x\",\"y\"]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "tag red: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("PUT", "/api/v1/tags", "{\"IDs\":[\"${blue}\"],\"Tags\":[\"y\"]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "tag blue: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/tags", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "tags: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0"), "x", "x")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "1"), "y", "y")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search?query=tag:y", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "count"), "2", "two tagged y: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search?query=tag:x", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "count"), "1", "one tagged x: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("PUT", "/api/v1/tags/x", "{\"Name\":\"renamed\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "rename: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/tags", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "0"), "renamed", "renamed: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("PUT", "/api/v1/tags", "{\"IDs\":[\"${red}\"],\"Tags\":[]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "clear red's tags: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/tags", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(string.trim(b), "[\"y\"]", "only y is left: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("DELETE", "/api/v1/tags/y", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete the tag: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/tags", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(string.trim(b), "[]", "no tags: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("DELETE", "/api/v1/tags/nosuch", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a tag that does not exist: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "tag not found: nosuch", "tag not found")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "total"), "2", "the mails are still there: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: deleting, with three mails "a", "b", "c" from the Send API.
        //   DELETE /api/v1/messages {"IDs":[<a>]} -> 200 "ok" ; GET /api/v1/messages -> total 2
        //   GET /api/v1/message/<a> -> 404 "404 page not found" (plain text)
        //   DELETE /api/v1/messages {"IDs":[<a>]} -> 200 "ok" (deleting what is gone is not an error)
        //   DELETE /api/v1/messages (no body: every message) -> 200 "ok" ; GET -> total 0
        spec.it("deletes selected messages, then all of them") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("deletes_selected_messages_then_all_of_them")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            a = send_mail_api("a", "a", "[]")
            send_mail_api("b", "b", "[]")
            send_mail_api("c", "c", "[]")
            st, b = mp("DELETE", "/api/v1/messages", "{\"IDs\":[\"${a}\"]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete a: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(string.trim(b), "ok", "ok")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "total"), "2", "two left: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/${a}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a is gone: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("DELETE", "/api/v1/messages", "{\"IDs\":[\"${a}\"]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "deleting it again: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("DELETE", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete all: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jnum(b, "total"), "0", "none left: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: the representative error statuses (Mailpit's errors are
        // JSON {"Error":..} for bad input and plain text for a missing route,
        // and it answers a wrong method with 404 too).
        //   POST /api/v1/send {"To":[{"Email":"b@x.com"}]} -> 400 {"Error":"error building message: from not set"}
        //   POST /api/v1/send {bad -> 400 {"Error":"invalid character 'b' looking for beginning of object key string"}
        //   GET  /api/v1/search -> 400 "Error: no search query" (plain text)
        //   GET  /api/v1/message/nosuchid -> 404 "404 page not found"
        //   GET  /api/v1/message/<an id of a message that exists>/part/9 -> 404 "404 page not found"
        //   GET  /api/v1/nosuch -> 404 "404 page not found"
        //   POST /api/v1/messages -> 404 (the path takes GET, PUT and DELETE)
        //   DELETE /api/v1/tags/nosuch -> 400 "tag not found: nosuch"
        spec.it("answers the representative error statuses") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("answers_the_representative_error_statuses")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            id = send_mail_api("exists", "e", "[]")
            st, b = mp("POST", "/api/v1/send", "{\"To\":[{\"Email\":\"b@x.com\"}]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a message with no sender: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "from not set", "from not set")
            st, b = mp("POST", "/api/v1/send", "{bad")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a body that is not JSON: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "invalid character", "invalid character")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/search", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a search with no query: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "no search query", "no search query")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/nosuchid", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a message that is not there: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/message/${id}/part/9", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a part that is not there: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("GET", "/api/v1/nosuch", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a path that is no endpoint: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("POST", "/api/v1/messages", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a method the path does not take: ${b}")
            st, b = mp("DELETE", "/api/v1/tags/nosuch", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a tag that is not there: ${b}")
            servirtium.end_recording(rec)
        }
    }

    if shared_container != null {
        e = tc.terminate(shared_container as *docker.Container)
        if e != "" { println("mailpit: removing the shared container: ${e}") }
    }
    return spec.run_summary(fw)
}
